# XZ Utils 5.8.3 tests/files: the .xz and .lzma half of its decoder test
# suite, 0BSD (tests/files/README). Not committed here: `cargo xtask xz-tests`
# fetches the release tarball pinned by SHA-256, and copies out exactly the
# files below after checking each one. 5.8.3 is years past the 5.6.0/5.6.1
# releases whose test files carried the CVE-2024-3094 payload; those two
# names are refused regardless.
#
# <file sha-256> <expected> <sha-256 of what xz 5.8.3 decodes it to, or -> <name>
#   good         decodes, to exactly those bytes
#   bad          must fail
#   unsupported  must be refused as unsupported
#   unverifiable an unknown check type: refused by default, decodes when the
#                caller allows an unverified decode (xz: warning, exit 2)
